al reentry facilities in the United States. It operates through three segments: CoreCivic Safety, CoreCivic Community, and CoreCivic Properties. The company provides a range of solutions to government partners that serve the public good through corrections and detention management, a network of residential reentry centers to help address recidivism crisis, and government real estate solutions. Its correctional, detention, and residential reentry facilities offer rehabilitation and educational programs, including basic education, faith-based services, life skills and employment training, and substance abuse treatment; food services; and work and recreational programs as well as health care services, including medical, dental, and mental health services. The company was founded in 1983 and is based in Brentwood, Tennessee.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Lucibeth N. Mayberry J.D. | President, CEO & Director | Age 53 | Compensation: $1.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 13K people. Revenue per employee of $162K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $4K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 11\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["CoreCivic, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $2.6B market cap on $2.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and +2% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $53M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.67\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 3.5\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 8.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 2.4% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (18.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.11862958381327925},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $11.0M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Broad market in a downtrend, trading below its 200-day average","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 45% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Liquidity Mapping Around (CXW) Price Events","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/11/Liquidity_Mapping_Around_CXW_Price_Events_112026030802_1795205282.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795205282.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How Investors May Respond To CoreCivic (CXW) Strong Quarter Lower Outlook","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/commercial-services/nyse-cxw/corecivic/news/how-investors-may-respond-to-corecivic-cxw-strong-quarter-lo","date":"2026-11-14","timestamp":1794676882.212,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.541,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"CoreCivic's (NYSE:CXW) Performance Raises Some Questions","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/commercial-services/nyse-cxw/corecivic/news/corecivics-nysecxw-performance-raises-some-questions","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794566471.582,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.402,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"CoreCivic (NYSE:CXW) Clears A Near-Term Line. What\u2019s Ahead?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/industrial/corecivic-nysecxw-clears-a-near-term-line-whats-ahead","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794494400.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.241,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"CoreCivic (CXW) Posts Strong Q3 Results, Is The Stock Still A Bargain?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/commercial-services/nyse-cxw/corecivic/news/corecivic-cxw-posts-strong-q3-results-is-the-stock-still-a-b","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794479587.395,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.836,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Responsive Playbooks and the CXW Inflection","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersda